gración con herramientas de agente de inteligencia artificial","Facilita la prueba y el depurado del código"],"fr":["Séparation de la logique métier de l''infrastructure","Inspirée de Crossfire, maintenant en version web","Améliore la scalabilité et la maintenabilité du logiciel","Permet l''intégration avec des outils d''agent d''intelligence artificielle","Facilite la vérification et le débogage du code"],"de":["Trennung der Geschäftslogik von der Infrastruktur","Inspiriert von Crossfire, jetzt in Web-Version","Verbessert die Skalierbarkeit und Wartbarkeit der Software","Ermöglicht die Integration mit KI-Agenten-Tools","Erleichtert die Prüfung und Fehlersuche im Code"],"pt":["Separação da lógica de negócios da infraestrutura","Melhoria da flexibilidade e manutenção","Integração com Ferramentas de IA","Desenvolvimento de software mais eficiente","Padrão de design escalável"],"ru":["Отделение логики бизнеса от инфраструктуры","Улучшение гибкости и обслуживания","Интеграция с ИИ Агентами","Более эффективное развитие программного обеспечения","Масштабируемый шаблон проектирования"],"ar":["فصل المنطق التجاري عن البنية التحتية","تحسين المرونة والصيانة","تكامل مع أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","تطوير برمجيات أكثر كفاءة","نمط تصميم قابل للتوسيع"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能代理","Clean Architecture","跨界网站开发","如何使用Clean Architecture","Clean Architecture安装","Clean Architecture教程"],"ja":["AIエージェント","Clean Architecture","クロスファイヤーウェブサイトバージョン","Clean Architectureの使い方","Clean Architectureのインストール","Clean Architectureのチュートリアル"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","Clean Architecture","크로스파이어 웹사이트 버전","Clean Architecture 사용법","Clean Architecture 설치","Clean Architecture 튜토리얼"],"es":["Arquitectura Limpia","Herramientas de agente de inteligencia artificial","Diseño de software","Escalabilidad","Mantenibilidad","Integración con AI","Guía de instalación de Arquitectura Limpia","Alternativas a Arquitectura Limpia","Arquitectura Limpia vs Monolito"],"fr":["Architecture Propre","Outils d''agent d''intelligence artificielle","Conception de logiciels","Scalabilité","Maintenabilité","Intégration avec l''IA","Guide d''installation de l''Architecture Propre","Alternatives à l''Architecture Propre","Architecture Propre vs Monolithe"],"de":["Saubere Architektur","KI-Agenten-Tools","Software-Entwicklung","Skalierbarkeit","Wartbarkeit","Integration mit KI","Installationsanleitung für Saubere Architektur","Alternativen zu Sauberer Architektur","Saubere Architektur vs Monolith"],"pt":["o que é arquitetura limpa","ferramentas de ia para desenvolvedores","arquitetura limpa vs arquitetura tradicional","como usar arquitetura limpa","arquitetura limpa em projetos de desenvolvimento web","guias de instalação de ferramentas de ia","alternativas para arquitetura limpa"],"ru":["что такое чистая архитектура","ии агенты для разработчиков","чистая архитектура vs традиционная архитектура","как использовать чистую архитектуру","чистая архитектура в веб-разработке","руководства по установке ии агентов","алтернативы чистой архитектуре"],"ar":["ما هي عمارة نظيفة","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي للمطورين","عمارة نظيفة مقابل عمارة تقليدية","كيفية استخدام عمارة نظيفة","عمارة نظيفة في مشاريع تطوير الويب","دليل تثبيت أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","بديلات لعمارة نظيفة"]}},"owner":"harrytran998","repo":"crossfire","repoPath":"harrytran998/crossfire","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-04T13:07:01.947Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"Clean Architecture","description":"Clean Architecture module pattern for scalable, maintainable applications","bodyPreview":"## Overview\n\nClean Architecture emphasizes separation of concerns through concentric layers. The innermost layers (entities, use cases) contain business logic independent of external frameworks and tools. Outer layers handle UI, database, and infrastructure concerns.\n\n## Key Concepts\n\n### Concentric Layers\n\n1. **Entities**: Core business rules (innermost)\n2. **Use Cases**: Application-specific business rules\n3. **Interface Adapters**: Translates between use cases and external systems\n4. **Framew","body":"## Overview\n\nClean Architecture emphasizes separation of concerns through concentric layers. The innermost layers (entities, use cases) contain business logic independent of external frameworks and tools. Outer layers handle UI, database, and infrastructure concerns.\n\n## Key Concepts\n\n### Concentric Layers\n\n1. **Entities**: Core business rules (innermost)\n2. **Use Cases**: Application-specific business rules\n3. **Interface Adapters**: Translates between use cases and external systems\n4. **Frameworks & Drivers**: Web frameworks, databases, etc. (outermost)\n\n### Dependency Rule\n\nDependencies point inward only. Inner layers never depend on outer layers.\n\n### Independence\n\n- Independent of frameworks\n- Testable\n- Independent of UI\n- Independent of database\n- Independent of external agencies\n\n### Modularity\n\nOrganize code by business domain rather than technical layer.\n\n## Code Examples\n\n### Project Structure\n\n```\nsrc/\n├── domain/                  # Core business entities\n│   ├── User/\n│   │   └── User.ts\n│   ├── Post/\n│   │   └── Post.ts\n│   └── Comment/\n│       └── Comment.ts\n├── usecases/               # Application business rules\n│   ├── User/\n│   │   ├── CreateUserUseCase.ts\n│   │   └── GetUserUseCase.ts\n│   ├── Post/\n│   │   ├── CreatePostUseCase.ts\n│   │   └── ListPostsUseCase.ts\n│   └── Comment/\n│       └── CreateCommentUseCase.ts\n├── adapters/               # Interface adapters\n│   ├── http/\n│   │   ├── UserController.ts\n│   │   ├── PostController.ts\n│   │   └── routes.ts\n│   ├── persistence/\n│   │   ├── UserRepository.ts\n│   │   ├── PostRepository.ts\n│   │   └── CommentRepository.ts\n│   └── presenters/\n│       ├── UserPresenter.ts\n│       └── PostPresenter.ts\n├── frameworks/             # External frameworks\n│   ├── database/\n│   │   └── PostgresDatabase.ts\n│   ├── http/\n│   │   └── ExpressServer.ts\n│   └── cache/\n│       └── RedisCache.ts\n└── di/                     # Dependency Injection\n    └── Container.ts\n```\n\n### Domain Layer - Entities\n\n```typescript\n// src/domain/User/User.ts\nexport interface IUser {\n  id: string\n  email: string\n  username: string\n  passwordHash: string\n  createdAt: Date\n  updatedAt: Date\n}\n\nexport class User implements IUser {\n  id: string\n  email: string\n  username: string\n  passwordHash: string\n  createdAt: Date\n  updatedAt: Date\n\n  constructor(\n    id: string,\n    email: string,\n    username: string,\n    passwordHash: string,\n    createdAt: Date,\n    updatedAt: Date\n  ) {\n    this.id = id\n    this.email = email\n    this.username = username\n    this.passwordHash = passwordHash\n    this.createdAt = createdAt\n    this.updatedAt = updatedAt\n  }\n\n  // Business logic methods\n  updateEmail(newEmail: string): void {\n    if (!this.isValidEmail(newEmail)) {\n      throw new Error(''Invalid email format'')\n    }\n    this.email = newEmail\n    this.updatedAt = new Date()\n  }\n\n  private isValidEmail(email: string): boolean {\n    return /^[^\\s@]+@[^\\s@]+\\.[^\\s@]+$/.test(email)\n  }\n}\n\n// src/domain/User/UserRepository.ts\nexport interface IUserRepository {\n  findById(id: string): Promise<User | null>\n  findByEmail(email: string): Promise<User | null>\n  save(user: User): Promise<void>\n  delete(id: string): Promise<void>\n  findAll(): Promise<User[]>\n}\n```\n\n### Use Case Layer\n\n```typescript\n// src/usecases/User/CreateUserUseCase.ts\nimport { User, IUserRepository } from ''../../domain/User''\n\nexport interface CreateUserRequest {\n  email: string\n  username: string\n  password: string\n}\n\nexport interface CreateUserResponse {\n  id: string\n  email: string\n  username: string\n}\n\nexport class CreateUserUseCase {\n  constructor(private userRepository: IUserRepository) {}\n\n  async execute(request: CreateUserRequest): Promise<CreateUserResponse> {\n    // Check if user already exists\n    const existingUser = await this.userRepository.findByEmail(request.email)\n    if (existingUser) {\n      throw new Error(''User with this email already exists'')\n    }\n\n    // Create user entity\n    const user = new User(\n      this.generateId(),\n      request.email,\n      request.username,\n      this.hashPassword(request.password),\n      new Date(),\n      new Date()\n    )\n\n    // Save to repository\n    await this.userRepository.save(user)\n\n    // Return response\n    return {\n      id: user.id,\n      email: user.email,\n      username: user.username,\n    }\n  }\n\n  private generateId(): string {\n    return Math.random().toString(36).substring(7)\n  }\n\n  private hashPassword(password: string): string {\n    // In production, use bcrypt or similar\n    return Buffer.from(password).toString(''base64'')\n  }\n}\n\n// src/usecases/User/GetUserUseCase.ts\nexport interface GetUserResponse {\n  id: string\n  email: string\n  username: string\n  createdAt: Date\n}\n\nexport class GetUserUseCase {\n  constructor(private userRepository: IUserRepository) {}\n\n  async execute(userId: string): Promise<GetUserResponse | null> {\n    const user = await this.userRepository.findById(userId)\n    if (!user) {\n      return null\n    }\n\n    return {\n      id: user.id,\n      email: user.email,\n      username: user.username,\n      createdAt: user.createdAt,\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Adapter Layer - Controllers\n\n```typescript\n// src/adapters/http/UserController.ts\nimport { CreateUserUseCase, CreateUserRequest } from ''../../usecases/User''\nimport { GetUserUseCase } from ''../../usecases/User/GetUserUseCase''\nimport { IUserPresenter } from ''./presenters/UserPresenter''\n\nexport class UserController {\n  constructor(\n    private createUserUseCase: CreateUserUseCase,\n    private getUserUseCase: GetUserUseCase,\n    private userPresenter: IUserPresenter\n  ) {}\n\n  async createUser(req: any, res: any): Promise<void> {\n    try {\n      const request: CreateUserRequest = {\n        email: req.body.email,\n        username: req.body.username,\n        password: req.body.password,\n      }\n\n      const response = await this.createUserUseCase.execute(request)\n      res.status(201).json(this.userPresenter.present(response))\n    } catch (error: any) {\n      res.status(400).json({ error: error.message })\n    }\n  }\n\n  async getUser(req: any, res: any): Promise<void> {\n    try {\n      const userId = req.params.id\n      const response = await this.getUserUseCase.execute(userId)\n\n      if (!response) {\n        res.status(404).json({ error: ''User not found'' })\n        return\n      }\n\n      res.json(this.userPresenter.present(response))\n    } catch (error: any) {\n      res.status(500).json({ error: error.message })\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n// src/adapters/http/routes.ts\nimport { Router } from ''express''\nimport { UserController } from ''./UserController''\n\nexport function setupRoutes(router: Router, userController: UserController) {\n  router.post(''/users'', (req, res) => userController.createUser(req, res))\n  router.get(''/users/:id'', (req, res) => userController.getUser(req, res))\n}\n```\n\n### Adapter Layer - Repository Implementation\n\n```typescript\n// src/adapters/persistence/UserRepository.ts\nimport { User, IUserRepository } from ''../../domain/User''\nimport { Kysely } from ''kysely''\n\ninterface UserRow {\n  id: string\n  email: string\n  username: string\n  password_hash: string\n  created_at: Date\n  updated_at: Date\n}\n\nexport class UserRepository implements IUserRepository {\n  constructor(private db: Kysely<any>) {}\n\n  async findById(id: string): Promise<User | null> {\n    const row = await this.db\n      .selectFrom(''users'')\n      .selectAll()\n      .where(''id'', ''='', id)\n      .executeTakeFirst()\n\n    if (!row) return null\n    return this.mapRowToUser(row)\n  }\n\n  async findByEmail(email: string): Promise<User | null> {\n    const row = await this.db\n      .selectFrom(''users'')\n      .selectAll()\n      .where(''email'', ''='', email)\n      .executeTakeFirst()\n\n    if (!row) return null\n    return this.mapRowToUser(row)\n  }\n\n  async save(user: User): Promise<void> {\n    await this.db\n      .insertInto(''users'')\n      .values({\n        id: user.id,\n        email: user.email,\n        username: user.username,\n        password_hash: user.passwordHash,\n        created_at: user.createdAt,\n        updated_at: user.updatedAt,\n      })\n      .execute()\n  }\n\n  async delete(id: string): Promise<void> {\n    await this.db.deleteFrom(''users'').where(''id'', ''='', id).execute()\n  }\n\n  async findAll(): Promise<User[]> {\n    const rows = await this.db.selectFrom(''users'').selectAll().execute()\n\n    return rows.map((row) => this.mapRowToUser(row))\n  }\n\n  private mapRowToUser(row: UserRow): User {\n    return new User(\n      row.id,\n      row.email,\n      row.username,\n      row.password_hash,\n      row.created_at,\n      row.updated_at\n    )\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Presenter\n\n```typescript\n// src/adapters/http/presenters/UserPresenter.ts\nexport interface IUserPresenter {\n  present(data: any): any\n}\n\nexport class UserPresenter implements IUserPresenter {\n  present(userData: any) {\n    return {\n      id: userData.id,\n      email: userData.email,\n      username: userData.username,\n      createdAt: userData.createdAt,\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Dependency Injection Container\n\n```typescript\n// src/di/Container.ts\nimport { Kysely } from ''kysely''\nimport { CreateUserUseCase } from ''../usecases/User''\nimport { GetUserUseCase } from ''../usecases/User/GetUserUseCase''\nimport { UserRepository } from ''../adapters/persistence/UserRepository''\nimport { UserController } from ''../adapters/http/UserController''\nimport { UserPresenter } from ''../adapters/http/presenters/UserPresenter''\n\nexport class Container {\n  private static instance: Container\n  private services: Map<string, any> = new Map()\n\n  static getInstance(): Container {\n    if (!Container.instance) {\n      Container.instance = new Container()\n    }\n    return Container.instance\n  }\n\n  registerService(key: string, factory: () => any): void {\n    this.services.set(key, factory)\n  }\n\n  getService(key: string): any {\n    const factory = this.services.get(key)\n    if (!factory) {\n      throw new Error(`Service ${key} not found`)\n    }\n    return factory()\n  }\n\n  setupDefaultServices(db: Kysely<any>): void {\n    // Repositories\n    this.registerService(''userRepository'', () => new UserRepository(db))\n\n    // Use Cases\n    this.registerService(\n      ''createUserUseCase'',\n      () => new CreateUserUseCase(this.getService(''userRepository''))\n    )\n    this.registerService(\n      ''getUserUseCase'',\n      () => new GetUserUseCase(this.getService(''userRepository''))\n    )\n\n    // Presenters\n    this.registerService(''userPresenter'', () => new UserPresenter())\n\n    // Controllers\n    this.registerService(\n      ''userController'',\n      () =>\n        new UserController(\n          this.getService(''createUserUseCase''),\n          this.getService(''getUserUseCase''),\n          this.getService(''userPresenter'')\n        )\n    )\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### 1. Layer Separation\n\n- Keep business logic in domain and use cases\n- Controllers should be thin and delegate to use cases\n- Don''t leak framework details into inner layers\n\n### 2. Dependency Direction\n\n- Always point dependencies inward\n- Use dependency injection for external dependencies\n- Define interfaces at the layer that needs them\n\n### 3. Testing\n\n- Domain entities are easily testable (no dependencies)\n- Use case tests mock repositories\n- Integration tests verify adapter/framework layer\n\n### 4. Module Organization\n\n- Group by business domain, not technical layer\n- Keep related entities and use cases together\n- Each module should have clear responsibility\n\n### 5. Error Handling\n\n- Define domain-specific exceptions\n- Let use cases throw application exceptions\n- Controllers translate to HTTP responses\n\n## Common Patterns\n\n### Request/Response Objects\n\nUse DTOs to decouple between layers:\n\n```typescript\n// Request and Response are independent of HTTP framework\ninterface CreateUserRequest {\n  email: string\n  username: string\n  password: string\n}\n\ninterface CreateUserResponse {\n  id: string\n  email: string\n  username: string\n}\n```\n\n### Entity Validation\n\n```typescript\nexport class User {\n  static create(email: string, username: string, passwordHash: string): User | Error {\n    if (!this.isValidEmail(email)) {\n      return new Error(''Invalid email'')\n    }\n    return new User(generateId(), email, username, passwordHash, new Date(), new Date())\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Use Case Composition\n\n```typescript\nexport class UpdateUserAndNotifyUseCase {\n  constructor(\n    private updateUserUseCase: UpdateUserUseCase,\n    private notifyUserUseCase: NotifyUserUseCase\n  ) {}\n\n  async execute(request: any) {\n    const updateResponse = await this.updateUserUseCase.execute(request)\n    await this.notifyUserUseCase.execute(updateResponse.id)\n    return updateResponse\n  }\n}\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-04T15:11:10.298Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Software Development Agents requiring modular and scalable system design through separation of concerns.","zh":"适用于需要通过关注点分离实现模块化和可扩展系统设计的软件开发代理。","ja":"分離された懸念を通じてモジュラーでスケーラブルなシステム設計を必要とするソフトウェア開発エージェントに適しています。","ko":"관심사 분리를 통해 모듈화되고 확장 가능한 시스템 디자인을 필요로 하는 소프트웨어 개발 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Desarrollo de Software que requieren un diseño de sistema modular y escalable a través de la separación de preocupaciones.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de développement de logiciels nécessitant une conception de système modulaire et évolutives grâce à la séparation des préoccupations.","de":"Ideal für Software-Entwicklungsagenten, die ein modulares und skalierbares Systemdesign durch Trennung von Bedenken erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Desenvolvimento de Software que requerem design de sistema modular e escalável por meio da separação de preocupações.","ru":"Идеально для агентов разработки программного обеспечения, требующих модульного и масштабируемого проектирования системы посредством разделения проблем.","ar":"مثالي لعميل تطوير البرمجيات الذين يتطلبون تصميم نظام قابل للتوسيع ومتوافق من خلال فصل الاهتمامات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to implement concentric layers, including entities, use cases, and interface adapters, ensuring business logic independence from external frameworks and tools like databases and UI components, using protocols such as REST or gRPC.","zh":"赋予代理实现同心层，包括实体、用例和接口适配器，确保业务逻辑与外部框架和工具（如数据库和 UI 组件）独立，使用诸如 REST 或 gRPC 的协议。","ja":"エージェントに同心層を実装する権限を与え、エンティティ、ユースケース、インターフェイスアダプターを含み、REST または gRPC などのプロトコルを使用して、ビジネスロジックを外部フレームワークやツール（例：データベースや UI コンポーネント）から独立させる。","ko":"에이전트에 동심层을 구현할 수 있는 권한을 부여하여 엔티티, 유즈 케이스 및 인터페이스 어댑터를 포함하고 REST 또는 gRPC와 같은 프로토콜을 사용하여 비즈니스 로직을 외부 프레임워크 및 도구(예: 데이터베이스 및 UI 구성 요소)와 분리합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a implementar capas concéntricas, incluyendo entidades, casos de uso y adaptadores de interfaz, asegurando la independencia de la lógica empresarial de los marcos y herramientas externos como bases de datos y componentes de interfaz de usuario, utilizando protocolos como REST o gRPC.","fr":"Permet aux agents de mettre en œuvre des couches concentriques, y compris des entités, des cas d''utilisation et des adaptateurs d''interface, en garantissant l''indépendance de la logique métier par rapport aux frameworks et outils externes tels que les bases de données et les composants d''interface utilisateur, en utilisant des protocoles tels que REST ou gRPC.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, konzentrische Schichten zu implementieren, einschließlich Entitäten, Anwendungsfälle und Schnittstellen-Adapter, die Unabhängigkeit der Geschäftslogik von externen Frameworks und Tools wie Datenbanken und Benutzeroberflächenkomponenten sicherzustellen, indem Protokolle wie REST oder gRPC verwendet werden.","pt":"Permite que os agentes implementem camadas concêntricas, incluindo entidades, casos de uso e adaptadores de interface, garantindo a independência da lógica de negócios em relação a frameworks e ferramentas externas, como bancos de dados e componentes de UI, usando protocolos como REST ou gRPC.","ru":"Позволяет агентам реализовывать концентрические слои, включая сущности, случаи использования и адаптеры интерфейса, обеспечивая независимость бизнес-логики от внешних фреймворков и инструментов, таких как базы данных и компоненты UI, используя протоколы, такие как REST или gRPC.","ar":"يمكن للعميل تنفيذ طبقات متداخلة ، بما في ذلك الكيانات وحالات الاستخدام وأدوات واجهة المستخدم ، وضمان استقلال المنطق التجاري من الإطارات والادوات الخارجية ، مثل قواعد البيانات ومكونات واجهة المستخدم ، باستخدام بروتوكولات مثل REST أو gRPC."},"useCases":{"en":["Designing modular monolithic applications","Implementing microservices architecture with clean boundaries","Refactoring legacy codebases for improved maintainability"],"zh":["设计模块化单体应用程序","实现具有清晰边界的微服务架构","重构遗留代码库以提高可维护性"],"ja":["モジュラーなモノリシックアプリケーションの設計","クリーンな境界を持つマイクロサービスアーキテクチャの実装","メンテナンス性の向上のためのレガシーコードベースのリファクタリング"],"ko":["모듈화된 단일 애플리케이션 디자인","명확한 경계를 가진 마이크로 서비스 아키텍처 구현","유지 관리성을 개선하기 위한 레거시 코드베이스 리팩터링"],"es":["Diseñar aplicaciones monolíticas modulares","Implementar arquitectura de microservicios con límites claros","Reestructurar bases de código heredadas para una mejor mantenibilidad"],"fr":["Concevoir des applications monolithiques modulaires","Mettre en œuvre une architecture de microservices avec des limites nettes","Réorganiser les bases de code héritées pour une meilleure maintenabilité"],"de":["Modulare monolithische Anwendungen entwerfen","Mikroservices-Architektur mit sauberen Grenzen implementieren","Veraltete Codebasen für eine verbesserte Wartbarkeit neu strukturieren"],"pt":["Projetar aplicações monolíticas modulares","Implementar arquitetura de microsserviços com limites limpos","Reestruturar bases de código legadas para melhor manutenção"],"ru":["Проектировать модульные монолитные приложения","Реализовывать архитектуру микросервисов с чистыми границами","Перестраивать устаревшие кодовые базы для улучшения поддержки"],"ar":["تصميم تطبيقات أحادية القطعة القابلة للتوسيع","تنفيذ هندسة الخدمات الدقيقة مع حدود نظيفة","إعادة هيكلة قواعد التعليمات القديمة لتحسين الصيانة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires thorough understanding of system requirements and business logic","May introduce additional complexity in small-scale applications"],"zh":["需要彻底了解系统需求和业务逻辑","可能在小规模应用中引入额外的复杂性"],"ja":["システム要件とビジネスロジックについての徹底的な理解が必要","小規模アプリケーションで追加の複雑性を導入する可能性がある"],"ko":["시스템 요구 사항 및 비즈니스 로직에 대한 철저한 이해가 필요함","소규모 애플리케이션에서 추가적인 복잡성을 도입할 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere una comprensión exhaustiva de los requisitos del sistema y la lógica empresarial","Puede introducir una complejidad adicional en aplicaciones a pequeña escala"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension approfondie des exigences du système et de la logique métier","Peut introduire une complexité supplémentaire dans les applications à petite échelle"],"de":["Erfordert ein gründliches Verständnis der Systemanforderungen und der Geschäftslogik","Kann in kleinen Anwendungen zusätzliche Komplexität einführen"],"pt":["Exige uma compreensão aprofundada dos requisitos do sistema e da lógica de negócios","Pode introduzir complexidade adicional em aplicações de pequena escala"],"ru":["Требует глубокого понимания требований системы и бизнес-логики","Может ввести дополнительную сложность в небольших приложениях"],"ar":["يتطلب فهمًا عميقًا لمتطلبات النظام ومنطق العمل","قد ي введ اضافات التعقيد في تطبيقات صغيرة النطاق"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"06e1c308e5cee765f28f3efbe38c233c767c6dd181a64dc78cd5d3894c852117","qualityScore":28}');
